window.FWN_MARTIAL_PEAK_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MARTIAL_PEAK_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":6101,"title":"Chapter 6101, Source Realm, Connecting All Worlds","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","The light was blinding, but it was over just as quickly as it appeared. What was once darkness due to everyone closing their eyes was now just darkness all around them.","Yang Ji, feeling the strange sensation that this place felt too familiar, used his Divine Sense instead of his eyes.","The moment of realisation struck and he widened his eyes in shock, “H-How are we here!?”","The Heavenly Demon Queen had managed to send them to the Source Realm. A place where it should only have been accessible through the Primordial Source Gate. More than that, they were at a truly familiar location. They were just outside of Mo Na Ye’s Black Ink Nest!","[How could a simple Array, even if it is a Grand Array, do something that Father couldn’t?] Yang Ji thought while in shock. Indeed, Yang Kai had to cross through the Primordial Source Gate to arrive here. He had no other methods. Not even the World Tree had the ability to send them over to a place like this.","Yet, the Heavenly Demon Queen had just done it.","This shock naturally extended to Yang Xu. It was only Yang Ling that remained confused, “W-Why is everything so dark!? Older Brother! Older Sister! Where are you!”","She panicked.","After all, this was no longer a Space they were used to. When Yang Ling tried to spread out her Divine Sense, it was blocked off. It seemed like there was a sphere covering her and another woman.","In fact, due to this sphere, Yang Ji and Yang Xu were unable to sense where Yang Ling was. Even her cries could not be heard.","Then, Wu Lun’s voice penetrated through. All three children could hear it.","“Stop crying. Geez, just got stuck with babysitting. Unbelievable. Look here, I have to keep you within a separate isolated space because you would have been tainted by the forces here. With your meagre cultivation, you would have lost sense of yourself once you step foot here. So, just wait and be quiet. Only I can hear you while you are within this sphere.”","Then, seemingly having made his point, he tuned out whatever Yang Ling would say.","The Heavenly Demon Queen then immediately turned to Wu Lun, “It would have been most prudent to preserve all of them together.”","“No way. These two can walk on their own. Only Mei Qing and this other brat needs my protection. Besides, I want them to see what happens. Or, are you telling me you don’t want them to see?” Wu Lun smirked and questioned.","The Heavenly Demon Queen just shrugged the question off. She turned forward and said, to an empty space in front of her. “We are cognisant that our presence has not escaped your notice. We beseech you to set aside any concerns regarding the welfare of the young ones. They will remain under our protection. We ask for safe passage to a secluded domain, far removed from your people. It is our intent to ensure no harm befalls onto your people.”","Soon, a presence appeared from the ground, full of darkness, like ink soaked its entire form. Naturally, this was Little Eleven. He had foreseen a day like this would come.","Though he knew many secrets of the world, he could not share them. Still, he understood what they were here for. After all, the Source Realm was the link between all Worlds. To describe it as the place of beginning would not be wrong, but would not be correct either. It was definitely the only site to easily reach that place.","Regardless, since things have come to this point, he knew any objections would not work. There was a youth, who even he could not see through. This could only mean one thing, and Little Eleven knew that any resistance was futile. He could only comply with their demands. It was already fortunate that this youth was not the one speaking, and the one leading the group was that little worm.","Little Eleven moved closer to the Heavenly Demon Queen. He asked, “How much distance?”","The Heavenly Demon Queen turned towards Wu Lun and the youth just shrugged, “The size of a third of your land would suffice. Just to be safe, double that and have everyone leave.”","Little Eleven did not so much as question why he needed such a large area. He just gave a nod and turned towards the Twins. He clenched his fist, concentrating all his might.","This time, even the ground started trembling a little as Little Eleven placed all his focus to condense two small beads.","It might have only taken a minute, but Little Eleven seems to be exhausted from this. The Twins could not fathom how much power was placed into these two small beads. However, when they received it with both hands and used their Divine Sense to survey it, they could not help but look perplexed.","After all, they could not feel anything from these beads.","Little Eleven made a small smile as he explained, “They are Black Origin Beads. They will show you the way home. Or at the very least, back to me. Keep them safe, and make sure you never expose them to others.”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu gave a nod and kept the beads into their Space Rings.","Yang Xu then asked, “Then what about Yang Ling? Won’t she need one?”","This time, Wu Lun finally spoke, “What for? She will be sticking to one of you. As long as you are with her, problem solved. Besides, this thing seriously cannot fall into the wrong hands, understand?”","It was the first time Wu Lun was being so helpful in explaining. Seeing his tone change, the Twin could not help but take it even more seriously.","Sensing that he was actually going a little out of character, Wu Lun immediately gave a cough “*Ahem.* Can you lead us away now?”","However, he was not directing this question to Little Eleven but to the Heavenly Demon Queen. After all, he did not wish to form any karmic connections to Little Eleven.","The Heavenly Demon Queen sighed and then turned towards Little Eleven, who snapped his finger and formed an Array beneath their feat using Black Ink Strength.","But, due to all the commotion, before the group got transported, from the window of the Black Ink Nest beside Mo Na Ye’s, two small eyes could be seen staring out.","When Yang Ji and Yang Xu turned because they noticed the presence of someone spying on them, those pair of eyes quickly vanished.","Little Eleven opened his mouth to say towards Yang Xu, “If Mo Na Ye were here, he would like to thank you for your gift. How unfortunate that he will not be able to see you two anytime soon.”","“It’s okay, we will come back one day. We definitely will.” Yang Xu said with a smile, though she was not exactly pleased to be forced to some unknown place.","Yang Ji added, “Uncle Eleven, you don’t need to worry. I’ll keep Yang Xu and Yang Ling safe,”","“Of course you will.” Little Eleven gave a brief smile and waved his hand. “Hope that fate will bring us together one day.”","Soon, darkness consumed the group and they got transported away, far away from any location they knew of.","It was a purely empty land, void of anything.","Afraid of the damage Wu Lun would inflict on this would territory, Little Eleven dare not even place them anywhere close to his territory. In fact, he dared not even transport them to the land of his adversaries, because he could not tell if Wu Lun might accidentally destroy his other two parts. So, he could only find a location void of everything, even other Profound Source Gates.","Wu Lun looked around and sighed, “Finally!”","He did not even need to take a look around. The instant he was transported here, he knew this was the perfect spot.","He spread his arms wide as though welcoming Heaven.","Then... an unbelievable scene played out. One which the Twins would never be able to forget.","*Crack*","Out of the darkness, akin to the abyss, light began to pour. Darkness retreated away, like soldiers that had lost all will to encroach upon this land. From above, cracks appeared.","These cracks were like spiderwebs, and there were multiple of them.","The light had simply poured in from these cracks, and it was enough to make the darkness retreat. Yet, this was only the beginning.","*Rumble*","The whole world seems to tremble and the cracks above spread further.","Soon, those spiderweb-like cracks burst apart, seemingly having the barrier of space shattered and from it came what seemed to be ginormous glowing golden fingers.","The glowing golden fingers pushed through whatever obstructed them. Anything in front of them was annihilated, disintegrated, as though the laws of this world themselves were being destroyed into oblivion.","Even when the world seemed to be desperately trying to mend itself, those fingers just pushed through.","Those five fingers grew longer, and eventually, an entire palm appeared. At this point, the world seemed to have finally faltered and broke. Now, not only was the sky cracking, all around them, space was cracking and distorting under the immense pressure.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu saw this hand coming towards them and could not help but panic. They instinctively heightened their guard but Wu Lun warned. “Don’t move. Stay where you are. This world is too fragile. I’m already trying to minimise the damage. One step further from me and you might die. Also, if I accidentally apply even more strength, your whole world will be in trouble, understood.”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu froze at those words. However, they could not help but have droplets of sweat fall from their backs. Even if the pressure was not directed towards them, they could still feel its crushing might from where they stood.","This hand, if it so wished, might truly be enough to destroy the world. Before it, they were different from ants.","The golden hand soon arrived, overcoming rejection from this world, and grasped the group in its palm.","However, before it scooped in, Wu Lun quickly covered everyone. He forced them all into the sphere Yang Ling was in. After all, at this point, it would be difficult to ensure everyone was safe from the immense pressure.","Worse off, even if the golden hand was gentle towards them, it could hardly contain its strength due to needing to continuously reject the laws of this world.","However, once it started to retreat, as though sentient, the world seemed to stop hindering its movement and allowed it to quickly pass. It was as though it was glad to quickly get rid of this invader.","Naturally, without this hindrance, the hand quickly left. It even went as far as to seal the gap it had created, lest something escape from it..."]},{"number":6102,"title":"Chapter 6102, Upper Realm","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","*Bang!*","It took merely the time to brew tea before Yang Ji and Yang Xu heard something break apart. The sphere that was protecting them, had broken off, dissipating into the air like it had never existed,","Now, exposed to being wrapped in the palm of a gigantic hand, Yang Ji, Yang Xu and Yang Ling did not feel any discomfort. At the very least, the earlier pressure had completely disappeared, else Yang Ling might not have been able to breathe.","However, Yang Ji and Yang Xu still felt uneasy. It was not fear, but there was some odd sensation within them that they could not explain.","At the same time, when they looked around, through the small cracks within the fingers of the clenched palm, they could not even see where they came from. However, what they could see was something odd, something they had never seen before.","Though merely a glimpse, they could see gigantic figures walking about. They were by no means close to where the Twins were, but their sizes were imposing to the degree where Yang Ji even wondered how such beings came to existence. In fact, the fist they were in was tiny compared to them.","Then, close to these figures, there was some glowing mist... Yang Ji and Yang Xu could not really make out what those mists are, but they must be incomparably large, since they were comparable in size to those giants.","“Wait... Brother, aren’t they... Giant Spirit Gods?” Yang Xu’s question made Yang Ji stunned for a moment.","“Are you serious? But, didn’t our Mothers say that there were only two left? How are there so many of them here? And, aren’t they even bigger than what they had described them to be?” Yang Ji solemnly questioned, his brain racing and questions after questions kept appearing.","“But, Brother, didn’t they say that the ones we have met are all similar to infants? Maybe, these are adult Giant Spirit Gods? Maybe... maybe they came here after they’ve outgrown our place?” Yang Xu said with her mind also wondering about.","Meanwhile, Yang Ling, not really understanding the issue here, just commented with a, “Wow...”","Wu Lun soon walked up to them and spoke, “Finally. Breaking through that boundary is such a pain, especially one that is so guarded.”","Then, Wu Lun turned to look at those Giant Spirit Gods and commented, “Seems like this is the first time you are seeing these giants. But close your jaws and focus. They are none of your business. At least, you should not even consider making contact with any of them. Right now, we need to talk about more important matters before we reach the Upper Realm.”","“Upper Realm?” Yang Ji and Yang Xu were hearing this term for the first time. Then, they noticed that someone could finally bring up this mysterious topic.","“Precisely, the Upper Realm.” The Heavenly Demon Queen, who understood their thoughts, chose to speak at this moment. “The Restriction has been dissolved now that we stand beyond the boundary’s reach. At long last, we may confer regarding our next endeavor. I must caution you, however, that we will not entertain all inquiries you might wish to raise. Certain matters are destined to remain shrouded in discretion. Even so, it is of paramount importance that you comprehend the course of events which shall now unfold.”","Strangely, this time, Wu Lun cut in. “Well, what she said. But, I will be the one to explain things here. Not here.”","He eyed the Heavenly Demon Queen, as though hinting her to back down.","The Heavenly Demon Queen, seeing this, wondered what he had in mind. However, since they were already away from the Grand Array she had modified, and his True Body had gotten involved, he does indeed hold the advantage in this discussion.","Seeing her silence and taking that as an agreement, Wu Lun continued with one finger raised, “First off, everyone here will not be moving together. More specifically, the girls will be together while the boy is with me. Understood?”","“Wait. Why? I don’t want to be separated from my Brother.” Yang Xu was quick to raise an objection.","However, Wu Lun quickly shot her down. “It’s for your safety. First off, know that beings from the Lower Realm are not welcomed in the Upper Realm. To those from the Upper Realm, you people are no different from slaves. No, worse than slaves. Just mere resources. And the aura you three have will definitely be a problem with how weak you three are.”","“We aren’t weak.” Yang Ji rebutted but his rebuttal only made Wu Lun scoff in ridicule. “Oh yeah? Try manipulating a small bit of Space here, why don’t you? Think my words are worth farts?”","“Huh!?” Yang Ji immediately started trying to manipulate Space Principles. However, he sensed as if something was impeding him. It was as if a fish had suddenly been moved to land but still tried to swim. Nothing moved.","Wu Lun rolled his eyes. “The Dao of Space that you know is nothing but a mere distilled, simplified form of the True Dao of Space. Naturally, that means the Principles you are used to controlling will not be found outside of your Lower Realm world. So, do not be mistaken in thinking that you are still strong here. In the Upper Realm, all three of you are lower than ants there, understood?”","This made the children start to worry. However, Wu Lun added while turning to the Heavenly Demon Queen, “Of course, we will be making sure you two are kept alive. For her, it’s a matter of survival. For me, I need you alive to be useful.”","“But you still haven’t explained to us why we have to separate.” Yang Ji asked.","“Because, either one of you will be carrying the Lower Realm Aura on them. When we first met, I could see that you two are deeply intertwined, as though your existences are as one despite being two completely different people. To be able to even share one’s mastery in a Dao must mean that the power that connects you two eclipses that of that Dao. If I’m not mistaken, you must be the one that’s proficient in the True Dao of Unity.” Wu Lun turned towards Yang Xu.","However, Yang Xu just seemed confused by this statement. After all, she had never cultivated a True Dao before. This connection with her Brother was an innate gift, as if Heaven and Earth had blessed them with such abilities. They had never heard anyone explain it off as the power of a True Dao.","However, as if dispelling all her doubts, the Heavenly Demon Queen added, “Indeed, she is the primary vessel.”","Wu Lun gave a nod then added while looking at Yang Ji, “Man, that makes things so much simpler. We will have one of you hold both of your Lower Realm Aura.”","Yang Ji rolled his eyes at how obvious Wu Lun was being. “But how will we do that? We can do that with Qi, our thoughts, memories and even insights. But we don’t even know what this Lower Realm Aura is.”","“Set your mind at ease. No effort is required of you. I have already arranged all that is needed.” The Heavenly Demon Queen stated and she dived into Yang Ji.","Moments later, Yang Ji and Yang Xu felt something was off within them. However, they could not tell what it was. Yang Xu felt like she had lost a little part of herself, while Yang Ji felt like his body was facing slightly more pressure from the world. It was apparent to Wu Lun though, as he said, “How convenient. One is completely devoid of the aura now. Pills would never be as effective as this. Heck, even Arrays would not fully be able to seal it in front of a true expert’s eye. Still, for now, no one would be able to tell that she is from the Lower Realm. Maybe that’s why ‘she’ has chosen to go with you...”","The final part of Wu Lun’s statement seemed to wander off, but he quickly brought himself back. “At least, for now, your Sister will be a lot safer in the Upper Realm. Heck, she might even be able to join a proper Sect. Though, there might still be some issues...”","Wu Lun seems to purposefully cut off there, as if urging Yang Ji to question him.","“What else?”","Wu Lun clapped his hands together and quickly stated without missing a beat. “You see, since your Sisters are going to be together, it will be difficult to ensure the little one’s safety unless they join a strong Sect. But, at Yang Xu’s current cultivation realm, I doubt she will be able to join.”","Yang Ji’s eye twitched. “Then, what do you want us to do?”","Wu Lun wiggled his finger. “No no no. Not so much what I want you two to do. Rather, it is what I want you to do.”","Wu Lun paused for a moment, as if awaiting Yang Ji to hold his breath before speaking, “I want you to transfer all your cultivation to her.”","““What!?””","Not only Yang Ji, but Yang Xu and Yang Ling all reacted the same way.","They were about to go to an unknown place, and this youth before them expected Yang Ji to pass off all his cultivation to Yang Xu? If this was not ridiculous, then what was?"]},{"number":6103,"title":"Chapter 6103, At Her Wits’ End","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","“How do you expect my Brother to survive if he doesn’t have his cultivation!?” Instead of Yang Ji lashing out, it was Yang Xu. She stared, wide-eyed in disbelief at what Wu Lun was proposing.","Wu Lun rolled his eyes, as if he heard the funniest joke in the world. “Do you think I’m not aware of what he can do? With that peculiar Phoenix Bloodline of his, I bet he can even regrow limbs if he needs to. What’s more, don’t think I don’t know you two have been cultivating your Physique and the various Daos in your spare time since you did not wish to focus too much on your cultivation realm. I’m not blind you know?”","Wu Lun continued, “Besides, you might think this is doing you a favour, but this is doing both of you a favour.”","Both Twins had eyes that clearly held partial doubts. Nevertheless, Wu Lun continued.","“Listen up. I’m sure you are already aware of this, but the Daos that you two have built your foundation upon are flawed. To even be able to stand shoulders to shoulders with the geniuses here, you can’t possibly build up your strength on loose sand. Regardless, one of you must be willing to walk this path anew. Else, neither of you will be able to keep up.”","“Yes, we will be sending you to a Sect, and yes, it will be safer there. But if you do not continue to prove your worth, do you think your Sister will be living in safety? The people there are not your Family. Heck, they aren’t even your friends. You think they won’t backstab you once you show limitations to your potential? Don’t be so naive you sheltered brats. This is not a game where we can live as we like. Do you think I’m not taking any sort of risk by taking you all out of your world? Do you think that ancient being inside of you isn’t taking a risk by manifesting now? We are all taking risks here. Don’t think you three can be the exception. The moment your Father has agreed to send you out is the moment he accepted that he might never see you all again. That is the risk you all have accepted when you all agreed to come out here.”","“Besides, I will be there with him. I too will not let him die before my goal is accomplished. So, let me ask you again, are you willing to start anew, and recultivate from scratch?”","Yang Ji looked at Yang Xu, and then Yang Ling. Honestly, to him, starting from scratch mattered little to the safety of these two. It took him less than twelve years to reach the Dao Source Realm. And, with the foundation of already climbing this hill once, the second time ought to be much faster. So, even when Yang Xu wished for him to refuse the offer, Yang Ji still gave a nod.","“Sure. I’m fine with starting all over. But, I don’t really know how to transfer my cultivation to Yang Xu. We’ve never done it before.”","“Not to worry. Once again, we will help you with that.” Wu Lun gave a nod and then he disappeared. However, before he did, he gave a smirk that Yang Ji would remember for eternity.","At the very next moment, Yang Ji was knocked unconscious.","As for Yang Xu and Yang Ling, they could barely react when Wu Lun appeared behind Yang Ji, knocking him out with one swift blow, catching him and placing him onto the golden ‘ground’. Then, he wrapped Yang Ji in his Qi, keeping him from waking up.","After all, with Yang Ji’s Phoenix Bloodline, one could expect him to wake up from such a strike within mere minutes.","“He already agreed to what you want. Why did you have to do that!?” Yang Xu questioned but Wu Lun sighed, “Then, would you like him to be awake and fully experience what it is like to have his cultivation sucked out of him?”","Yang Xu went silent then said, “If you expect me to help you, then I’m not doing it.”","“Even when he himself has agreed to it?” Wu Lun stated, more coldly this time. “In that case, would it be better for me to cripple his cultivation instead and make him start out as a cripple? I’m sure you’d do whatever you can to salvage his Qi before it completely gets wasted, if not for yourself, at least to salvage what you can to return it to him.”","“You! Didn’t you just say that you aren’t going to let him die!?” Yang Xu’s eyes turned red at this point.","“And crippling him doesn’t mean he is dead, right?” Wu Lun sharply stated and reminded, “I do not wish to waste words with you. Don’t play politics with me. You’re just too young. Either you do what I say, or I cripple him and no one walks away any better. I need him as a blank slate, as much as you need his cultivation to enter that Sect with commendation.”","“You!” Yang Xu was about to rush up to Wu Lun but the youth simply raised a single finger and pressed down.","Yang Xu was immediately pressed down by the pressure of what seemed to be a thousand mountains. All movements forward immediately ceased as she could only use all her strength to resist being crushed. She could not even look up, her head barely able to hold up.","Yang Ling at this point reacted by rushing forward to her Sister. However, how could she possibly help in any way? She was quickly pushed away, with one gentle flick from another of Wu Lun’s finger.","Then, Wu Lun’s voice came, this time, only Yang Xu could hear it. This was in fact to prevent Yang Ling from learning about any of the following statements.","“The True Dao of Unity. Sounds grandiose, but, if one person is above the other, is that truly unity? You two were born, bound together, but is that really the case? I wonder how much of it is what he wished for, and how much of it is what you wish for him to be?”","Wu Lun said with his eyes narrowed. “What you are afraid of isn’t him merely losing his cultivation. What you are afraid of is the lack of this link between the two of you. After all, this mysterious link between the two of you is built upon not just your shared births, but some mysterious cultivation technique as well. Though I do not know what exactly this cultivation technique is, if one side is stronger than the other, it will not balance out. It will do him more harm than good. While he pursues the various Daos, you’ve been solely focused on this one, have you not, that’s why you are much better than him at the True Dao of Unity.”","“You can lie to him, even lie to yourself, but you can’t pretend in front of my eyes. I’ve been observing you two for quite some time now. Compared to how proficient you two are in the Dao of Space, your Dao of Time hasn’t truly caught up. You two barely used it. With your Dragon Bloodline, this should have fallen to you to focus on cultivating it. But, you’ve been relying mostly on your Bloodline’s natural aptitude. So, of course this Dao has fallen behind.”","“Let him go and one day, you two might stand as equals once more. No. I will force you to.” Wu Lun stated.","Yang Xu remained muted, still strongly defying him.","“Unlike myself, he bears no connection to the fate of your existence. He is unburdened by morals in the pursuit of his objective. He has spent countless aeons devoted to a solitary, unwavering purpose. Do not harbour the illusion that your silence shall serve as deterrent or persuasion.” The Heavenly Demon Queen spoke up at this moment in Yang Xu’s mind.","“Shut up! Both of you! You two purposefully dragged Yang Ling along to be taken as a hostage! Yet, you two dare to preach to me!” Yang Xu commended the Heavenly Demon Queen in her mind.","However, the Heavenly Demon Queen was not angered by her statement. In fact, as though she had already predicted such an outburst, she calmly continued without so much as a missing beat. “You have, upon occasion, labelled me a parasite. Yet one must ask: wherein lies the distinction between us? You attach yourself to your Brother with such desperation that his existence becomes as vital to you as the very air you breathe, all while he remains wholly self-sufficient, fine to separate, even willing to lay down his cultivation for your sake.”","“I will not bring harm to my Brother, unlike you!” Yang Xu screamed in her mind. “I can’t let him be the only one taking on such risks! I have to be there with him!”","“What harm have I brought upon either of you? And you dare speak of not harming your Brother? Your very existence has already rendered him a marked target in the Upper Realm. Furthermore, your present obstinacy may well result in him being crippled.” The Heavenly Demon Queen continued, “That man will not cease. He will truly cripple him unless you do as told.”","“And how did we even get into this mess!? This is all because of you!” Yang Xu screamed some more, and she continued to scream but... what else could she do?","She was at her wits’ end."]},{"number":6104,"title":"Chapter 6104, Woke Up Naked","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","Yang Ji opened his eyes in a state of confusion. Looking up from below, he could clearly see the familiar blue sky up above. However, he felt his body was far heavier than what it should be, and far colder as well. Not to mention, his back and bottom both felt a little cold and moist.","“Oh, you’re finally up.”","Soon came a familiar voice, one which Yang Ji could never forget. After all, this was the same voice from the youth who had knocked him out before he was in this state.","Lying down, Yang Ji tried to look to his sides, but he saw no one. Then again, the voice seemed to be directly entering his mind, so Yang Ji presumed that Wu Lun must be somewhere far away. Until...","“Stop looking around. I do not have my physical form at the moment. Can’t get exposed, you know. I’m on your chest.”","“Huh?” Yang Ji exclaimed and looked down. Only now did he realise why everything was so cold.","He was naked!","“What the!” Yang Ji hurriedly jumped up, stumbling a little due to the unfamiliar weight on him. He quickly looked around and saw that his fingers did not have the Space Ring his Parents had given him. In fact, on him, there was nothing but a boring looking string necklace, with a ring attached.","The ring was nothing remarkable. It did not have any marks on it. It was just a band, like someone took a thin metal cylinder and drilled a hole through it.","With his precious jewels out in the open, Yang Ji quickly hid them with his hands and looked around again to make sure there was no one around him.","“Relax. No one is around to see you buttnaked. Besides, who would be interested in a child– you know, never mind.” As if realising something, Wu Lun quickly changed topic. “Just scrap up some big leaves and tie them around your body.”","“Where are my clothes? Wait. Where are we in the first place? Why are you now just a ring? Where are Yang Xu and Yang Ling? You didn’t make them go around naked as well, did you!?” Yang Ji suddenly realised there were more pressing questions than his clothing as he hurriedly shot questions after questions.","“Hey hey hey, move your mouth less and move your hands more. I will answer your questions as you create your new attire, alright? I don’t particularly enjoy seeing your naked jewels as well, just so you know.” Wu Lun said as matter-of-factly, causing Yang Ji to momentarily open his mouth and then shut it.","The boy soon moved to a nearby bush, which had quite large leaves. Just one leaf would be enough to wrap around half of his waist.","Yang Ji soon moved his hands to try to pluck a leaf out but...","“Huh?”","The leaf could not be torn. Even as he tried with all his strength, with veins popping out of his forehead, the leaf simply would not get torn off.","“Did you forget that your cultivation has been completely transferred onto your Sister?” Wu Lun, seemingly exasperated, reminded.","“But, don’t I still have my Physique? Why. Won’t. This. Leaf. Come off” Yang Ji pulled, and pulled but it all seemed to fail.","“Did you forget where I’ve sent you? We are now in the Outer Heaven, which is within the Upper Realm. We’re no longer in your Lower Realm World. Everything here is not just a tier or two tougher than the materials in your world. They are on a whole other level of existence. Even with your trained Physique, it doesn’t mean you can do whatever you want over here.” Wu Lun sighed and explained patiently.","“Instead of some fresh leaves, just use those that have fallen to the ground.”","Yang Ji, already feeling his hands sore from all the pulling, did as he was told. Truly, instead of plucking fresh leaves, it was so much easier to pick those that had fallen to the ground.","“To think I can’t even take leaves from a plant now...” Yang Ji remarked, a little taken aback by how weak he had become.","“In the first place, who taught you to pull? A normal person would have sliced it from the side...” Wu Lun, realising that he was dealing with a sheltered child, now knew how much work they had to cover. “Also, you don’t need to worry that much about being weak. A normal child borned and raised here also would not be able to pull a leaf out with just their physical strength.”","“Really?”","“Well, they would use Qi for it. But, it’s not like you can use it right now.” Wu Lun added, which only served to annoy Yang Ji since he knew that too.","However, the boy just focused on gathering and tying up some leaves instead of commenting much. Not to let Wu Lun annoy him.","Seeing Yang Ji was being boring, Wu Lun continued to explain their current situation.","“You’ve been sent to the Outer Heaven, while your Sisters have been sent to the Central Heaven. I wish I could have you start off in the Central Heaven as well, but that would be making you seek death in your current state. But well, not like the Outer Heaven lack opportunities for you. As long as you can grasp them, you will eventually be able to see your Sisters again.”","“How long would that take?”","“Depends on you. If you’re strong enough, then we can just go. But right now, you need to build up your whole foundation first. As for why I didn’t allow you to take any of your items from your world, it’s simple: those things will not just expose your identity, and the world you are from, they can also hinder you. You Sisters likewise cannot take anything on them made from your world.”","Hearing that, Yang Ji accidentally used too much force and snapped a dried up leaf.","Seeing this, Wu Lun continued, “Don’t worry. Unlike you, they aren’t naked. Those girls have to maintain appearances in the Central Heaven, or others would take advantage of them. Your Sister can pose as a Young Lady from some powerful Family with the things I’ve passed onto her. With how much she snapped back at me while you were knocked out, I’m sure she can play her role fine. After all, she has a truly haughty overseer with her.”","At this point, Yang Ji could let out a sigh of relief. At least, his Sister had items on them to assist them in case they got into trouble. Though he was still worried, they at least have some kind of safety net. Unlike him, butt naked in the wild, with only a talking ring to accompany him.","“If you could have given her stuff, you could have left me with something, at the very least.” Yang Ji complained.","However, Wu Lun seemingly scoffed. “You don’t even know what the Outer Heaven is like. If I give you something precious like that, you think you’ll be left alone? You, with no Qi to use those Artifacts in the first place? You can’t fully protect yourself, and you want to put a target on your back?”","“But you could have at least left me some clothes...” Yang Ji said as admittedly, the cold ground on his bottom and jewels reminded him of how harsh nature was to the uninitiated.","“Look. I don’t have anything that looks vile enough to make people leave you alone, alright? Anyways, with where we are going, honestly, any clothes that I give you would be in tatters pretty much instantly.” Wu Lun spoke as if everything he did had a reason for it. “Why do you think I took on such a dull form? It’s so no one would want to steal me from you.”","“Now that you mention it, why are you not here in person? What’s with this form of yours?” Yang Ji questioned as he tied some leaves together and tried to put them on. It did fit, albeit a little loose. He also felt a little less exposed, truly only a little less exposed as the small wind beneath his loins reminded him of this fact. [I guess this will do...]","“To simply put it, I cannot physically join you. Like, it would seriously cause you more harm than good if people realise your relationship with me. That’s why I tried my best to leave as small a mark of my existence on your Sisters as possible.” Wu Lun said while seemingly shrugging his shoulders. Though Yang Ji could not see the youth at the moment, he could certainly feel as though that was what Wu Lun would do.","“Wait. Then, it’s fine if it is with me?” Yang Ji questioned, a little bewildered by this.","“Yeah. If not, I wouldn’t actually agree to do this with that ancient being in you two.” Wu Lun said and paused for a moment.","“It seems to be about time.”","“Huh? Time for what–”","At that exact moment, the ground suddenly shook. It was strong enough to cause Yang Ji, who had barely gotten used to his current strength, who could no longer fly, to stumble onto the ground.","Yang Ji soon closed his eyes and used his Divine Sense, which thankfully could still be used due to his Knowledge Sea still being present. After all, if one were to remove one’s Knowledge Sea, that would be no different to leaving a person brain dead, if not have their Soul extinguishing.","Off in the distance, not too far from him, Yang Ji could feel an immense concentration of energy. This energy was unfamiliar to him. In fact, if Yang Ji still had his cultivation and tried to sense the World Energy here, he would come to realise that it was no longer the same World Energy that he was used to.","Nevertheless, this blast of energy struck the sky as if announcing to the world that something world changing was happening.","Wu Lun in the ring, seemingly enjoying the look of astonishment on Yang Ji’s face, gave a smirk and said. “That’s where we need to go. To build up your foundation before you even start cultivating, we need to head there.”","At those words, for some reason, instead of fear, Yang Ji felt his heart race with anticipation."]},{"number":6105,"title":"Chapter 6105, World of Wonders","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","“Oh?” Yang Ji exclaimed and started dashing forward with excitement.","However, as if to pour cold water over the youth, Wu Lun warned. “Hey, hey, hey. Who told you to directly head there?”","*Pa* Seemingly maybe because he was still not used to his current strength, or maybe it was because he was too taken aback by those words, Yang Ji managed to slip and his face got planted into the soft leaf litter on the ground.","Thanks to the soft, rich nutrient ground, Yang Ji did not get injured, but his whole face and body certainly got a new makeover. If one were to call him a beggar, he would find it hard to dispute those words.","“Ahh...” Muttering a sigh and expressing his various emotions all at once, Yang Ji looked up from the ground and started to complain, “Why didn’t you tell me beforehand, before I started running?”","“What are you talking about? That was all on you. I didn’t tell you to move, did I? Don’t blame me for how you lost your balance.” Wu Lun jabbed and he continued to explain, “Listen up. You are currently no different from a baby walking through a deathtrap. You think you’re the only one who noticed that disturbance? You might be able to tear through Space and directly arrive at the spot in an instant back then, but now you need to move through a forest, full of hidden dangers, on foot. You can’t possibly expect yourself to stay safe if you rush forward like this.”","“You say all that, but aren’t I still headed there in the end?” Yang Ji stood up and dusted off the leaves on his face. He even checked his new ‘clothes’ to see if they had dropped off, or got damaged.","It was fortunate that they still held on. Else, he had to remake it again...","“*Tsk tsk tsk*. It’s not the same. Your Divine Sense is limited right now. But, if you directly head over there, you would need to cross over the territory of another Divine Spirit.” Wu Lun warned him. “Don’t forget your identity as a Divine Spirit. Though you tend to prefer your Human Form more, seeing as your Parents keep to their Human Forms, you can’t forget this key identity of yours.”","Yang Ji, upon hearing this, understood what Wu Lun was trying to explain. After all, Divine Spirits, Ancestors of the Monster Race, naturally held some traits that were passed down. One of those was the consumption of other Divine Spirits to help one cultivate. Though Yang Ji had never done this before, he had heard from Mother Shan Qing Luo that it was dangerous for young Divine Spirits to roam about on their own because of this.","This warning was more towards Yang Ji’s Brothers and Sisters. But right now, he had to heed it with greater awareness, since he now lacked the ability to tear through Space at will.","“Okay. Okay. I get it. I need to be more careful. But, some of what you are saying doesn’t make sense. If there is a Divine Spirit there, then wouldn’t this whole forest be filled with Divine Spirits? I’m sure even the place I’m in is someone else’s territory.” Yang Ji questioned while he turned around to look, scanning the place once more with his Divine Sense.","“It depends on whose territory you’re in. Also, there’s no way I would throw you into some Tiger’s den in the state you’re in.”","“You say that, but didn’t you throw me here butt naked?”","“Hey hey, lighten up. There’s a reason as to why I do certain things. Right now, you are in a safe territory, mainly because the one who rules over this part of the forest doesn’t bother with lower beings like you. In short, you are an Ant not worth taking the effort to stomp on. But for the one upfront, that one is a little greedier. Even if Ants can’t fill the gaps between its teeths, it will still take a bite.” Wu Lun shrugged and said it matter-of-factly. It was as though he had intimate knowledge of the situation here.","“In that case, what am I supposed to do?” Yang Ji questioned.","“Just follow my lead. It’ll take about three days to get there. And, don’t worry. The opportunity will still be there. Also, during this time, do not cultivate, understand? You will travel solely using your physical body.” Wu Lun delivered the task as though a Master assigning his Disciple to pick up water from the river.","“Yeah yeah.” Yang Ji conceded and did as he was told.","The journey, though, was far harsher than what Yang Ji had initially thought.","The route he had to take did not just consist of the natural footpath on the ground. He was made to jump from tree to tree, swim through rapids, scale up cliffs, glide through the air using a huge leaf, dive down into a lake, move through underwater caverns... and the list went on...","Yang Ji, who already looked dishevelled after his first fall, was unrecognisable now. If he met with a beggar, even they would take pity on him at this point. His only ‘clothes’, the one he made, had broken apart who knows how many times, had been stitched together who knows how many times.","Still, the only thing that seemed to deceive this sorry state of his was that his skin held no marks of any injuries. This was not because he did not get injured. He did, multiple times, and had accumulated scratches and bruises. However, with his Phoenix Bloodline, he naturally recovered from all of such wounds within minutes.","At the same time, Yang Ji listened to whatever Wu Lun said to the letter, and abided by whatever he told him. This was not because he fully trusted Wu Lun, but rather, he could feel that he was gradually becoming stronger over time. The gains were by no means massive, but Yang Ji could feel that he had overall gained better control over his body compared to when he first came to the Outer Heaven.","Also, when he had spent time moving about, he felt strange... more able to appreciate the world around him. When Yang Ji thought about it, his adventures with Yang Xu had been quite rapid and quite effortless. He could move from one spot and another with just his thoughts, and the place he had visited would be ingrained within him such that he could always revisit it inside of his dreams.","This was technically the first time he was putting so much effort and time into going to a singular destination. Furthermore, the scenery of the places he had so far traversed was interesting.","Mountains and rivers did not flow like normal. Sometimes, rivers could flow upstream, and mountains did not need to connect to the lands beneath them.Trees came in all different shapes, colours and sizes, with some so big Yang Ji could not even reach their leaves unless he wanted to take a day or two to scale them.","He had even seen a river flowing from a tree’s branch to the trunk and then to the ground downstream. Beasts that flew in the air that dwarfed him hundreds of times. In just only three days, he had probably seen more here than his lifetime back home.","If he could, he definitely wanted to show all these sights to Yang Xu. However, right now, with their connection cut off, he could only wait until the day they could meet once more.","Still, for that day to come, he would need to establish his foundation first. And with Wu Lun’s words, Yang Ji knew that day would be today.","“We’re here. Up there.”","“Huh? Are you serious?” Yang Ji questioned as if Wu Lun was joking. However, the response he got was absolute, as though Wu Lun was thinking, ‘what the heck is this kid talking about?’","“Of course. It’s up there.”","Yang Ji stared at the scene in front of him in confusion.","In front of him was a floating island. This time, the water that flowed from it cascaded down like torrents, bashing the ground below.","[Wait. If it’s floating, then how did that earthquake even come about?] Yang Ji wondered as he looked to spot a few oval shaped shadows moving to and fro from this floating island.","“You can’t be expecting me to swim up that waterfall, right? It’s not heading up this time, you know.” Yang Ji reminded Wu Lun, who seemingly rolled his eyes.","“Of course not. If you happen to be scaling the waterfall when that island falls, you’d be crushed.”","“Erm... I think I will be crushed even if I’m on top of the island, if that happens.” Yang Ji seemed unwilling to budge on this issue.","“Relax. I’ve guided you all the way here. Do you think I don’t have a way for you to get up?” Wu Lun said in a relaxed manner. “Just wait a moment. Your ride will be here soon enough.”","“Huh?” Yang Ji murmured as he looked around. However, what he did not realise was that close to his feet, behind him, there was a shadow that was getting bigger..."]},{"number":6106,"title":"Chapter 6106, Blood Binding Seal","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","Yang Ji, sensing that something was quickly coming at him from above, did not even turn around to check. He immediately took evasive manoeuvres and ran to the side.","*Bang!*","Soon, a relatively small Spirit Ship came crashing down. ‘Relatively small’ because it was definitely not the usual sized Spirit Ship Yang Ji had seen before. Even from a distance, it was obvious the ones flying to and from the floating island were definitely a lot bigger than this ship.","Still, it was apparent that this small Spirit Ship was certainly made with luxury in mind. Every inch of it was decorated by jewels if not ornaments. If this did not scream, ‘I’m rich’, Yang Ji did not know what did.","Naturally, such a Spirit Ship had to have its own passengers. And, true to its size, there were only three passengers.","“Young Mistress!” A deep voice could be heard roaring from inside. It was so powerful that Yang Ji could not help but shield his ears.","[That actually hurt me!?] Yang Ji was slightly taken aback by this. After all, it was just a simple emotional roar. It held little to no intention to harm anyone. Yet, he got injured?","Wu Lun’s voice soon reminded him. “Later, do not show any sort of hostility, regardless of what they do. Understand?”","“Seriously, can’t you just tell me what they are going to do?” Yang Ji word off using his Divine Sense. However, as expected, no response came back.","Soon, one passenger after another came out. There was a man, a woman, and a child. The man and woman were obviously not couples, from how distant they were from one another. Especially, when the man was carrying the child as he moved out of the wreckage, and the woman was apologetically lowering her head towards the man.","All three were dressed well. Of course, anyone would be ‘dressed well’ compared to Yang Ji. It was just that there was clear opulence on how they dressed. It was not like they wore large jewelry, but the material they wore certainly highlighted wealth and prestige. Still, the man and woman could not be compared to the child that was being carried. That one child, from Yang Ji’s perception, was covered in Artifacts from head to toe.","Yang Ji did not know how valuable these Artifacts were, but he could somehow see his younger Siblings in this child. His Mothers certainly gave them too many Artifacts to use, so some were used as toys and some as clothes. This child seemed to be similar.","The man who stood with an unconscious child in his arm, turned towards the woman, who was lowering her head apologetically. “Xing Ting, raise your head. If you wish to apologise for your folly, then protect the Young Mistress till the end. If she dies, you know what will become of us and our Families. A thousand deaths will not suffice to quell Master’s wrath.”","The woman, Xing Ting, looked up with resolve in her eyes. “Understood.”","The man, seeming to nod, turned his attention elsewhere. His eyes turned sharp and his hand moved to grasp something in the air.","The very next instant, Yang Ji felt an indescribable pulling force. Tried as he might, this was not a force he could overcome. Unable to resist, he was pulled all the way to the man’s hand, with his neck being held in a choke hold.","*Ghh*","“A child?” The man’s eyes scanned Yang Ji with cold disregard. He seemed to ponder, all while Yang Ji was being choked, trying to claw the hand on his neck open but his nails tail at even making a scratch.","Xing Ting gave a nod, and she turned back to the crash site, “Sir, what if we leave a corpse behind as a decoy?”","The man’s eyes soon turned back to the woman and a violent pressure pressed her down. She could not help but kneel at that moment. “Do you take them for fools? For them to target us, they are certain to have some method to track the Young Mistress. They would definitely know if she is alive. Such paltry tricks would not work on people of their calibre.”","The man soon turned back to Yang Ji, “But, we do indeed need to buy time.”","“No clothes, no cultivation, that ridiculous thick stench of the Lower Realm. An abandoned child of the pathetic invaders here. Be thankful you get this opportunity to serve a higher being in sacrificing your life.” The man coldly said as he released his grasp on Yang Ji. However, Yang Ji was not free. In fact, the same force that pulled him over seemed to have locked him in place, up in the air.","After all, how could a child without any cultivation possibly have transverse the barrier between the Lower Realm and the Upper Realm? It was far more likely for him to be a spawn between a couple who had invaded into the Upper Realm, and had settled here. Furthermore, seeing as how this child did not have any cultivation at his age, it was more likely that he could not cultivate. For such trash, it was obvious what the couple would do–abandon him in the wilderness to let fate decide what to do with him.","The man moved his hand and grasped towards the Spirit Ship. Very quickly, boxes were opened up. Inside them were clothes..","The man soon clenched his hand and Yang Ji found that his body was starting to get moist. In fact, surpassing his Divine Sense, there was some kind of power that was gathering moisture in the air, and compressing it onto his body. It first started as droplets, but as thousands upon thousands of them gathered, they soon formed into a sphere large enough to completely cover him.","When enough water was gathered, Yang Ji was soon mercilessly spun within this water bubble. All manner of dirt and grim was cleaned from his body, as did his consciousness. Even the leaf overall he wore for the past three days had been completely torn apart by this merciless spinning.","Still, it was not over. Once deemed clean enough, the man snapped his finger and all water had completely evaporated off his body, leaving a cleaned boy exposed to all the elements.","“Help him get dressed. I need to prepare the seal.” The man ordered and he stepped aside to lay the unconscious girl down on the ground.","Yang Ji, still dizzy from all that spinning, tried his hardest to try and escape while the woman was busy picking clothes for him.","Wu Lun reminded him again, “Do not resist. Just let matters take their course.”","Yang Ji, who was doubting those words, tried to take a step away, but the man’s warning came despite his eyes being closed, and his focus being on his Young Mistress as he made a small cut to draw some blood from her. “Brat, it is meaningless to try and escape. Serve your purpose and maybe you will get a chance at freedom. If not, crippling your legs would not be an issue.”","Yang Ji scoffed in his mind, [Even if you break my legs, it’ll just take me a couple of weeks to recover. Better to just leave.]","However, Yang Ji knew that with the disparity in strength, he would certainly be caught if he did anything. So, Yang Ji wanted to open his mouth to speak, but was quickly silenced by Wu Lun.","“If you try to propose some kind of condition, he will just seal your voice. Even worse, he will seal your movements. At this stage, you won’t be able to break those seals even if you destroy and regenerate those body parts. So, just act obedient even if your heart is defiant. I can only advise you. I can’t aid you more than this right now.”","Yang Ji soon rolled his eyes in his heart. “Fine. I’ll do as you say. It seems like you’ve predicted this would happen.”","To not be suspected, he transitioned his mouth opening as an opportunity to puke. Even his small retreat could be taken as him moving to one side to puke.","Seeing this, the man gave a scoff, and focused all his attention back onto the Young Mistress.","Meanwhile, the woman, seeming to hold no prejudice against those from the Lower Realm, quickly wiped Yang Ji’s mouth and helped him put on a dress, even equipping him with some Artifacts to make the disguise more convincing.","She even tried to take the ring necklace away, since it was something their Young Mistress would never wear. However, upon seeing how reluctant Yang Ji was to part with it, she convinced herself that this might be the only thing his Parents had left behind and could not find it in herself to remove it. Besides, it was small and could be kept well concealed. So, it was not too much of an issue.","Still, there were obvious points that made Yang Ji different from the Young Mistress. After all, one was a boy and the other was a girl. Even if their ages were similar, their builds and hair length was different. If one was observant enough, it would be easy to spot these differences. In fact, even their auras were different. Not considering their individual auras, Yang Ji had the thick aura of the Lower Realm, which made him stand out even amongst others from the Lower Realm.","To solve the biggest issue, which was their aura, they first had to hide the Lower Realm aura clinging onto Yang Ji. For that, they used a ring Artifact.","Seemingly to match with its purpose, its design was rather bland compared to all the Artifacts the Young Mistress wore. It was a golden ring with runes on it that were carved within the ring. When worn, it would just look like a band ring.","Naturally, its true purpose was to hide one’s aura. It was not meant to be used to hide the Lower Realm aura. Still, it should be effective enough to at least deceive their pursuers.","As for their builds and hair, the man gave his apology before cutting off his Young Mistress hair to match that of Yang Ji. Then, he took the hair and mixed it inside the blood he collected.","After muttering something incoherent, he used his finger to draw in the air, using the blood as base and the hair as a brush. The man easily created a seal and planted it into Yang Ji’s body.","After he was done with the ritual, the man coldly said to Yang Ji, “Now that the Blood Binding Seal is done, if the Young Mistress dies, you will suffer the same fate. If you survive through this ordeal, we will naturally release the Blood Binding Seal. So, now you have no choice but to cooperate with us.”"]},{"number":6107,"title":"Chapter 6107, Defiance City","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","Yang Ji looked at the man with obvious defiance in his eyes. However, since the Blood Binding Seal was already done, there was nothing this child could do about it. The man just scoffed, “I like the look in your eyes, make sure you are as defiant against death then.”","The man did not bother with Yang Ji any further. He would leave matters to Xing Ting. “Take him to the city, where you can hide. With the Blood Binding Seal, if they are tracking us using Young Misstress’ aura, they will approach him thinking he is the Young Mistress. If not, and it is worse than I hope, that someone in the Family has betrayed us and is chasing after us, I need to remain by the Young Mistress’ side.”","“Understood. I will hide out in the city.” Xing Ting said but was quickly rebuffed by the man. “No. There is no point in hiding out like a rat. We have a decoy here with us. He will play the role of a decoy. You will do as what should have been done for the Young Mistress. Make sure he checks into the Revitalisation Inn.”","“But Sir, we only have a limited quota and the Young Mistress needs the Pool of Revitalisation. If he enters...” Xing Ting wanted the man to reconsider, but he added.","“No need to worry over such matters. I can handle getting another quota. We are, after all, in the Outer Heaven. There are plenty of ways to get my hands on another quota.” The man said with his fist tightening, showing that his fist was another method he would use if needed.","“Understood...” Although still reluctant to do as told, Xing Ting abided by the order.","“Now, go get the kid and get him out of here while I stall those still after us.” The man declared and gently picked up the Young Mistress, before putting her inside a box, clearly to hide her whereabouts, if not to protect her from the aftershock of the upcoming battle.","Then, the man made a few chants, and wrote a few things in the air, before leaping up into the air and roaring, “COME! ALL YOU DOGS, COME AND FACE DEATH!”","Very soon, up in the air, beams of light could be seen gathering around the man. They were distant enough that Yang Ji could barely make out their figures. Those beams of light were obviously those people chasing after the man, Xing Ting and that Young Mistress.","Yang Ji did not know why they were gathering from other distant places, converging to one spot. However, if he had to make a guess, it might be that the Spirit Ship they were on, the one that crash landed, might not have been the only Spirit Ship those people were after.","While looking up, Yang Ji did not notice that Xing Ting had been observing him all the while. The woman was reluctant to take care of another child besides her Young Mistress, but more than that, she felt that this child that had taken up was more than meets the eye.","As if to prove her point, what child would look up at the battle of experts, with eyes not of awe or inspiration, but rather that of pure curiosity and bewilderment. It seemed as though Yang Ji was studying them rather than watching them.","And indeed, Yang Ji was doing as her intuition was saying. He was truly studying the different techniques those in the sky were employing. Even if distant, even if they were just vague figures, the methods they employed were truly eye opening. He wondered if he could do them one day.","For example, how the man created the Blood Binding Seal or that protective layer that protected the box the Young Mistress was in. Yang Ji had never even seen such techniques before. They were so abstruse, he merely saw the man drawing in the air. Yang Ji could not grasp the concept behind those moves, or what he had written.","It was obvious that some other Principle was at play, something that the 3,000 Worlds lacked.","The battle above was exactly that. What seemed to be Artifacts, of varying shapes, were being used. Techniques that did not solely rely on weapons, sound was a weapon, sight was a weapon, even one’s drawings could be used as weapons. Fists? Using fists was to be expected, but there was an expert up there making strange hand gestures before delivering a punch, executing it and making glowing rings appear around his wrist.","All manner of techniques Yang Ji had never seen before were being played out up above. Upon seeing such a scene, Yang Ji could not move his eyes away.","Still, it was not like Yang Ji could be allowed to enjoy the show for much longer. As if impatient at him for not moving, Xing Ting finally spoke up, “We’re moving.”","She did not hesitate to carry Yang Ji away, in a princess carry, leaving behind the real Young Mistress on the ground, hidden in a box. With a single leap, she easily flew into the air, covering kilometres in one go.","Yang Ji did not bother himself with whatever this woman was doing. Besides, he was already being dressed as a girl, being carried like this did not matter much. His Mothers and Sisters did this when he was younger as well–dressed him like a princess for fun. Right now, he just wanted to carry on watching the battle.","He could not help but ask Wu Lun, using his Divine Sense, “Will I be able to do that someday?”","“‘That’? What do you mean? You need to be more specific.” Wu Lun responded.","“You know, the ability to draw something and then have it contain some kind of power.”","“You mean the power of Runes? Ah, well, hard to say. Some of these things are based on one’s affinity with the True Dao. The True Dao of Runes is actually closely related to the True Dao of Spirit Arrays. Like in your world, one needs to have the amplitude to be able to comprehend such Daos.” Wu Lun said honestly, without any mincing of words. “But what makes this more interesting compared to all the others? They are using a wide variety of Techniques, showcasing various True Daos.”","“It just seemed like the hardest to learn.” Yang Ji confessed, there was no particular reason for it, except that this seemed like the most challenging one to learn.","At this point, Wu Lun seemed to be in deep thought over something, but he no longer spoke. Likewise, Yang Ji did not continue to ask. After all, part of the fun in taking on a challenge was discovering this mystery on his own. Like the Dao of Space, even if he and Yang Xu had Yang Kai’s advice from time to time, most of his own mastery over this Dao was from his own discoveries.","So, he continued to watch the battle with intent, studying the different runes the man made to cause golden chains to wrap around his enemies.","However, these chains were too weak to keep those true experts at bay. With the Artifacts in their disposal, how could they be kept contained with a simple Technique?","Out of the eight figures besieging the man, two had broken free from their restraints and they continued to attack. One kept the man busy, while the other tried to free the other collaborators.","Yang Ji watched on, not paying attention to any of the others besieging the man. He was solely focused on the man and how his hand moved.","Unfortunately, Xing Ting was far too fast. She easily made it up the floating island and placed Yang Ji down, grabbing his attention. “Follow me.”","Her tone was cold as she refitted the cloth around his head, which was an Artifact used to hide one’s appearance. She grabbed his hand after she was done, tugging him forward into the site Wu Lun wanted Yang Ji to go...","Defiance City.","One of the few cities within the Outer Heaven, founded based on the Pool of Revitalisation.","Out of all the cities in the Outer Heaven, Defiance City was relatively small. However, it could be considered one of the more prosperous cities. After all, this was a city that even people from the Inner Heaven might visit.","However, when there was light, there would always be darkness. Due to the discrimination against those of the Lower Realm, there was a clear distinction between those of a higher class and those of a lower class.","Upon landing on the floating island, outside the city, the first sight that greeted Yang Ji was not the prosperity of the city, but rather the remnants of what the city did not want. In other words, dilapidated settlements outside the city walls.","In response, Yang Ji could only nod.","Seeing such a sight, Yang Ji could not help but get taken aback and stop for a moment. However, Xing Ting continued to drag him through the area. She explicitly warned him, “Do not speak, do not look at any of them. Young Mistress must never be found to be associated with such beings.”"]},{"number":6108,"title":"Chapter 6108, Lower Realm Denizens","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","As he walked past building after building, he naturally took note of the living conditions of these ‘unwanted people’. It was... tragic. Even when in board daylight, Yang Ji could see people stealing from others. In fact, it was easy to spot pools of blood on the ground from time to time, with clusters of people begging, if not lying there seemingly close to death.","There were even children, seemingly even younger than him, but hardly had flesh on their bones, only skin. They were so malnourished that it even shocked Yang Ji.","These children seemed to lack the strength to even play. They sat on the streets, begging if not trying to steal. However, one thing that he took notice of was, on the street lane they were walking on, no one, not even the adults, dared to get close to Yang Ji and Xing Ting. Even those begging, knowing that this might be a chance for a meal, dared not approach the pair.","Yang Ji naturally found this to be quite odd. When looking up ahead, the same treatment was held towards those who dressed well. All these people would avoid coming into contact with those that walked on this straight lane.","Still, Yang Ji was quite curious, so he asked Wu Lun, “Why are they just loitering around here? Some of them seem to be starving. Even if they are beggars, back home, they would still approach us and ask if we could spare them something. There is also a whole entire forest down below. I’m sure they could get food from there.”","Wu Lun, had his voice a little lowered, maybe a bit emotional from this scene, explained, “They have no choice but to remain here. Every single one of them is tied to this island. They can’t leave.”","“Huh? Why? I didn’t feel any barriers when I entered. They shouldn’t be trapped here.” Yang Ji questioned. Looking up and behind, there certainly were no barriers that prevented him from entering or exiting.","“You are thinking too simply. There are much better methods to keep people in place, rather than walls and Arrays.” Wu Lun said.","“Better?”","There was a sigh as Wu Lun coldly said, “A Seal for Bloodlines, to be eternally tied to a piece of land. With this floating island, it is easy to declare its borders. What’s more, if these people ever procreate, all their offspring would be tied to this land as well. A seal that will live on, without needing maintenance, as it feeds on their Life Force to sustain itself and propagate through the generations. How terribly efficient. Truly.”","“Wait, there are even such things? Then, if I touch any blood on the ground, would I be bound to this land as well?” Yang Ji frowned as he looked at those puddles of blood on the floor, some of which had already turned brownish because no one bothered to wipe away the blood and had just left it there to rot.","“You don’t need to worry about that. These Seals are bound to that person till death. They die out the moment the blood no longer remains within their bodies. Even if you drink blood directly from their wrist, it will not affect you. Still, if you want to try, you’re more than welcome to.” Wu Lun smirked.","Yang Ji shook his head and looked forward as they approached a large wall. This wall was tall, akin to a mountain, separating the floating island’s outer dilapidated region.","Past a gigantic gate, Yang Ji could see the buildings inside. They were pristine and grand, a stark contrast to the area outside the wall. Just from a glimpse from the outside, Yang Ji could already feel a strong sense of grandeur.","Xing Ting led Yang Ji to a queue. It was a line that was filled with people who were dressed well and proper. The robes they wore were definitely made of rare materials. Yet, they still paled in comparison to the dress Yang Ji was currently wearing. From this, Yang Ji could easily tell that the Young Mistress that he was acting as, must have been some truly important figure. At least, despite her young age, she already held status higher than the people here.","Meanwhile, on another side of the gigantic gate, there was another line packed with people. However, this queue was not for people of status, but for those who seemed to be from the outer region of the floating island.","“Oh? They are actually allowed inside?” Yang Ji remarked, slightly surprised since the inner region was so different from the outer region. Furthermore, there seems to be a deep-seated hatred for the people of the outer region.","“Of course. Why else would the city want to keep these people? They are useful slaves.” Wu Lun added. “For generations, they have lived like this. Maybe it was they themselves who had escaped from the confines of their Lower Realm World, but if they were too weak or unlucky, and got caught, all those people from the Lower Realm would end up like this.”","“You’re saying that Yang Ling and Yang Xu might end up like this!?” Yang Ji reeled back. He did not think that the situation for Lower Realm denizens were this horrendous in the Upper Realm.","Wu Lun rolled his eyes. “Relax. Your Sisters are safe. You gave up your cultivation, and took on all that Lower Realm Aura from your Twin to keep them safe. This, I can guarantee you. Right now, Yang Xu will seem no different from a native of the Upper Realm, and Yang Ling and be treated as her maidservant. It’s the best disguise they can have. Besides, no one would expect someone of the Lower Realm to ever enter the place they are in.”","“Right now, you have only one thing you need to focus on, which is to build up your foundation so that you can start cultivating again. Your Sisters can wait.” Wu Lun reminded.","Hearing this, Yang Ji gave a nod. He was truly too weak to do anything right now. Even if he were to look for them, he would only be a burden to them.","While conversing with Wu Lun, the line moved and Yang Ji unconsciously moved along with it. Eventually, it was their turn to enter the gate.","“Next” The guardsman announced and Xing Ting walked up to present a Token to the guard.","However, the moment the guard saw that Token, his eyes widened. There was a flash of fear, which was quickly hidden to the best of his ability and he had to excuse himself, asking another guard to head in to report, while he himself greeted Xing Ting with a far more respectful tone, “Greetings, how may I assist you?”","Xing Ting, cold and icy, did not speak. Instead, she took out a piece of paper with a written note on it and a seal.","Once the guard saw it, his eyes turned sharp and he gave a nod. “Understood. I’ll prepare the transportation for our two honoured guests.”","With that, he led them in, and to the side, while having another guard replace him to continue supervising the entrance of visitors.","As they moved, the guard leading them picked up a black Token with some Rune on it. The Token glowed with a mysterious light before the guard kept it once more. Obviously, this black Token must have functioned as both the guard’s identity and a communication device.","And, as the guard was focused on some other matter, Xing Ting’s eyes turned sharp. She communicated using her Divine Sense, her voice directly entering Yang Ji’s head. “Boy, we need to be careful from here. We cannot trust anyone from this place. The guards here were more fearful than welcoming. They might actually have a hand in attacking our Young Mistress. So, you cannot trust them, understood?”","“U–”","Just as when Yang Ji was about to respond, Wu Lun quickly jumped in. “Stop! Are you trying to expose yourself?Just continue pretending you can’t use your Divine Sense. You are now acting as someone who can’t cultivate. Don’t make them suspicious.”","Yang Ji was once more reminded of the current persona he had picked up–a Mortal boy, abandoned by his Lower Realm Parents because he could not cultivate. If he had exposed the fact that he could use Divine Sense, that might suggest he had been keeping his cultivation hidden. Yang Ji did not know what would happen if the truth came to light, but he would rather not find out.","Xing Ting’s grip tightened as she walked with Yang Ji, along the path the guard was leading them down. Up ahead, there was a carriage already prepared for them.","When Yang Ji first saw the carriage, his eyes widened. It was not because the carriage was luxurious looking, with crystal and gold-like metal adorning it. What Yang Ji was taken aback by were the things pulling the carriage. They were not Monster Beasts or Divine Spirits. Rather, they were Humans!","Six men, dressed shabbily, obviously no different from those outside the wall. In fact, these might be people directly taken from outside the wall. Aligned in two rows with their hands bound to the handle used to push the carriage, these men waited for their passengers to board.","These slaves were now being treated no different from horses or cattle. Logically, since they had cultivation, and were strong themselves, it was certainly a waste not to use them, no?","Nevertheless, this difference between expectation and reality left Yang Ji stunned. He momentarily froze up, which caused Xing Ting to lightly pull his hand to move him forward.","“So, this is the Upper Realm...” Yang Ji silently muttered to himself. It certainly was... an interesting sight to see."]}]);
